{"content":[{"c":["BEMA*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Greek term for a judgment seat or tribunal of a Roman official. Although the term also means “to step” or “stride,” it was used in the first century ",{"c":["AD"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"}," primarily to denote an elevated area or platform (reached by steps) from which political orations or judicial decisions were made. Excavations in the city of Corinth have revealed a large, elaborately decorated ",{"c":["bema"],"sourceClass":"greek","t":"span"}," located in the center of the marketplace."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["In the NT, Jesus was questioned before the judgment seat of Pilate (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.27.19","r":"Matt.27.19","rawR":"Matt.27.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.27.19","value":"Matt.27.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 27:19"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=John.19.13","r":"John.19.13","rawR":"John.19.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.19.13","value":"John.19.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jn 19:13"},"). Herod Agrippa I addressed the people of Tyre and Sidon from a ",{"c":["bema"],"sourceClass":"greek","t":"span"}," (",{"href":"?bref=Acts.12.21","r":"Acts.12.21","rawR":"Acts.12.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.12.21","value":"Acts.12.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 12:21"},"). The apostle Paul was brought before the tribunal of Gallio in Corinth (",{"href":"?bref=Acts.18.12-17","r":"Acts.18.12-17","rawR":"Acts.18.12-17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.18.12-17","value":"Acts.18.12-17"}],"t":"ref","v":"18:12-17"},") and again before Festus’s tribunal in Caesarea (",{"href":"?bref=Acts.25.6,10,17","r":"Acts.25.6,10,17","rawR":"Acts.25.6,10,17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.25.6,10,17","value":"Acts.25.6,10,17"}],"t":"ref","v":"25:6, 10, 17"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["In two passages, Paul used the term to refer to God’s judgment seat. In ",{"href":"?bref=Rom.14.10","r":"Rom.14.10","rawR":"Rom.14.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rom.14.10","value":"Rom.14.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Romans 14:10"}," he warned those who would arrogantly judge others that all must stand before the tribunal of God. According to ",{"href":"?bref=2Cor.5.10","r":"2Cor.5.10","rawR":"2Cor.5.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Cor.5.10","value":"2Cor.5.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Corinthians 5:10"},", the merits of each person’s work will be determined before the judgment seat of Christ (cf. ",{"href":"?bref=1Cor.3.13-15","r":"1Cor.3.13-15","rawR":"1Cor.3.13-15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Cor.3.13-15","value":"1Cor.3.13-15"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Cor 3:13-15"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Judgment_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Judgment_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Judgment_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Judgment"},"; ",{"href":"?item=JudgmentSeat_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"JudgmentSeat_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"JudgmentSeat_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Judgment Seat"},"; ",{"href":"?item=LastJudgment_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"LastJudgment_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"LastJudgment_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Last Judgment"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Bema","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Mt 27:19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.27.19","rawQueryValue":"Matt.27.19","sourceRefExact":"Matt.27.19"},{"anchorText":"Jn 19:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=John.19.13","rawQueryValue":"John.19.13","sourceRefExact":"John.19.13"},{"anchorText":"Acts 12:21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Acts.12.21","rawQueryValue":"Acts.12.21","sourceRefExact":"Acts.12.21"},{"anchorText":"18:12-17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Acts.18.12-17","rawQueryValue":"Acts.18.12-17","sourceRefExact":"Acts.18.12-17"},{"anchorText":"25:6, 10, 17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Acts.25.6,10,17","rawQueryValue":"Acts.25.6,10,17","sourceRefExact":"Acts.25.6,10,17"},{"anchorText":"Romans 14:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Rom.14.10","rawQueryValue":"Rom.14.10","sourceRefExact":"Rom.14.10"},{"anchorText":"2 Corinthians 5:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Cor.5.10","rawQueryValue":"2Cor.5.10","sourceRefExact":"2Cor.5.10"},{"anchorText":"1 Cor 3:13-15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Cor.3.13-15","rawQueryValue":"1Cor.3.13-15","sourceRefExact":"1Cor.3.13-15"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"962c0cc7fc2562d37d84cca5d3141fcd6c1c83bf86d720d97365398b1cda84f7","sourceItemName":"Bema","sourceItemOrder":170,"sourceMember":"Articles/B.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Bema","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Bema*","title":"Bema*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}